    "id": "UgyDm_Sz43gH5yjiiGF4AaABAg",
    "parent": "root",
    "text": "The \"How the Advisors Are Built\" section is the real lesson. The roast only lands because each persona is grounded in how that person actually decides — Wickman asks who owns the issue, Buffett asks what the downside is. Skip that grounding and you get generic advice with famous names pasted on. It's the same rule in the systems I build for business owners: an agent's output is capped by the judgment you encode into it upfront. The debate format just makes the trade-offs visible instead of averaging them into mush.",
