    "parent": "root",
    "text": "What I find tricky with this process is that, no matter how you get to a decision, the human will only apply it when they agree with it. If the roast room agent tells you to sell your house and all-in spacex stock, will you do it? The lacking piece is rarely how to make AI arrives a smart decision, you know it's LLM behind the scene and they are not responsible to anything they say. And that's why you can't build trust, thus it doesn't matter the decision comes from a roast-room or gpt-3.5",
